Package: TDecisionCodigo
Title: Decision Theory: Uncertainty, Multicriteria and Bayesian Methods
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Pedro Luis", "Luque Calvo", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), email = "calvo@us.es")
Author: Pedro Luis Luque Calvo [aut, cre, cph]
Maintainer: Pedro Luis Luque Calvo <calvo@us.es>
Description: Perform decision analysis as taught in undergraduate statistics
    courses, covering classical criteria under uncertainty,
    pairwise-comparison and outranking multicriteria techniques, and
    Bayesian decision trees. Compute expected values, value-of-information
    measures, entropy and channel information, as well as Analytic Hierarchy
    Process (AHP), ELimination Et Choix Traduisant la REalite (ELECTRE),
    Preference Ranking Organization METHod for Enrichment of Evaluations
    (PROMETHEE) and Axiomatic Arrow-Raymond rankings. Provide helpers to
    build decision and valuation matrices, homogenise criteria and summarise
    results in tables and plots for teaching and applied work with 'R'.
